===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, relating to, or suggestive of [[war#Noun|war]]; [[warlike]].
#* Dryden
#*: But peaceful kings, o'er '''martial''' people set, / Each other's poise and counterbalance are.
# Relating to or connected with [[armed forces]] or the [[profession]] of [[arm#Noun|arms]] or [[military#Adjective|military]] [[life]].
#* '''1938''', [[w:Xavier Herbert|Xavier Herbert]], ''[[w:Capricornia (novel)|Capricornia]]'', New York: D. Appleton-Century, 1943, Chapter XII, p. 194, [https://archive.org/details/capricornianovel00herb]
#*: He was lying on the table with head pillowed on the broken concertina and body sheltered with the Federal Flag, looking like a '''martial''' corpse.
# Characteristic of or befitting a [[warrior]]; having a military [[bearing#Noun|bearing]]; [[soldierly]].
#: {{synonyms|en|soldierlike|warriorlike}}
# {{lb|en|chemistry|medicine|obsolete}} Relating to, or containing, [[iron#Noun|iron]]; [[chalybeate]].
#: {{ux|en|'''martial''' preparations&emsp;'''martial''' flowers (a reddish crystalline salt of iron)}}

